READING:
  Theta(x) . polylog = Otilde(x).  The 2-term fit over the stable band
  (n=14..24) gives alpha = 1.012 ~ 1.0 with a POSITIVE polylog
  exponent d = +0.721; the forced-alpha=1 model mul ~ x*(log2 x)^0.87
  predicts every per-step ratio to sub-percent.  The per-step ratios
  DECLINE monotonically (4.471x -> 4.329x) toward
  4.0 -- the fingerprint of a polylog-dressed LINEAR term, NOT a super-
  linear power (a pure x^a has a CONSTANT ratio).  The single-power alpha
  reads up to ~1.07 on the high-n window purely from the (log x)^0.9
  dressing -- the exact artifact S512's 2-term fit defeats.  CONFIRMS
  mem_hierarchy_wall's IDEAL=4.0 op-count leg out to n=24 (x~1.7e+07).
  fmul share of wall: --wall-timing OFF (S530 measured ~78%); the
  op-count above is exact and timing-independent.
